#, c-format
msgid ""
"Sends technical reports that do not contain personal information. Data is "
"collected by %1$s (<u><a href='%2$s'>privacy policy</a></u>)."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: the parameter here is the name of a distribution,
#. * like "Fedora" or "Ubuntu".
#.
#: gnome-initial-setup/pages/privacy/gis-privacy-page.c:79
#, c-format
msgid ""
"Sends technical reports that do not contain personal information. Data is "
"collected by %s."
msgstr ""
"Magpadala ng mga ulat teknikal na hindi naglalaman ng personal na "
"impormasyon. Kinokolekta ng %s ang datos."

#: gnome-initial-setup/pages/privacy/gis-privacy-page.c:123
#, c-format
msgid ""
"Allows apps to determine your geographical location (<u><a "
"href='%1$s'>privacy policy</a></u>)."
msgstr ""

#: gnome-initial-setup/pages/privacy/gis-privacy-page.c:174
#: gnome-initial-setup/pages/privacy/gis-privacy-page.ui:14
#: gnome-initial-setup/pages/privacy/gis-privacy-page.ui:28
msgid "Location Services"
msgstr "Serbisyo sa Lokasyon"

#: gnome-initial-setup/pages/privacy/gis-privacy-page.ui:17
msgid ""
"Turn on location services to let applications know your geographical "
"location."
msgstr ""

#: gnome-initial-setup/pages/privacy/gis-privacy-page.ui:56
msgid "Automatic Problem Reporting"
msgstr "Awtomatikong Pag-uulat ng Problema"

#: gnome-initial-setup/pages/privacy/gis-privacy-page.ui:99
#: gnome-initial-setup/pages/ubuntu-insights/gis-ubuntu-insights-page.blp:134
#: gnome-initial-setup/pages/appearance/gis-appearance-page.blp:138
msgid "You can change this later in the Settings app"
msgstr ""

#: gnome-initial-setup/pages/software/gis-software-page.c:123
#: gnome-initial-setup/pages/software/gis-software-page.ui:11
msgid "Third-Party Repositories"
msgstr "Repositoryo ng mga Third-Party"

#: gnome-initial-setup/pages/software/gis-software-page.c:125
#, c-format
msgid ""
"Third-party repositories provide access to additional software from selected "
"<a href='%s'>external sources</a>, including popular apps and drivers that "
"are important for some devices. Some proprietary software is included."
